# Env files are a loaded weapon (KEEL P4). Never committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# Daily price capture output (D-036). Not in git: it is data, it grows every
# trading day, and it belongs in Postgres once a price migration exists.
#
# WHERE IT ACTUALLY LIVES: the price-data branch, published daily by
# .github/workflows/capture-prices.yml. Ignored HERE on main, committed THERE.
# An orphan branch, so it shares no history with the project and can be dropped
# wholesale once a price migration loads it into Postgres.
#
# BUT NOTE, and this is the one place ignoring a directory carries real risk:
# this is the only data in the project that CANNOT be re-fetched. Facts reload
# from immutable FSDS archives; a lost capture day is gone at any price. Until
# it is loaded into the cluster it exists in exactly one place, so it needs a
# backup that is not this repository. See docs/reports/2026-09-25-price-capture-built.md
price_capture/
